# Risk Analysis and Business Continuity Management Project

## Overview

This repository contains the documentation and analysis developed as part of a group project focused on identifying, evaluating, and mitigating business and information system risks across various industries. The project aligns with key learning objectives in information security and continuity management, addressing both technical and strategic perspectives.

## Objectives

The project aimed to:

- Correlate the context of a company to the risks it faces in the process of doing business.
- Identify and analyse business, environmental, and information security risks across diverse industries.
- Explore and evaluate risk mitigation solutions, considering cost, implementation complexity, and user impact.
- Connect identified risks to business continuity and disaster recovery planning.
- Demonstrate ethical information use by distinguishing between original contributions and cited sources.

## Key Deliverables

- Risk assessment reports tailored to different industry contexts
- Proposed risk mitigation strategies with comparative evaluation
- Business continuity impact analysis
- Supporting research and documentation

## Technologies & Tools

- Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel)
- Risk Matrix Templates
- Research Databases and Citation Tools

## Contributors

This project was completed collaboratively by a student group as part of academic coursework. Contributions include analysis, documentation, research, and presentation preparation.


